A||N||4||pdqfiero||2.8 to 3.1 conversion question||||11||
Z||000000||pdqfiero||07-29-2000||06:18 PM||||I am having a heck of a time with this. The Fiero online service guide says that the only blocks that the 3.1 crank will work in are the ones with certain 3 letter codes on the side following the numbers 2.8. Well mine says 2.8 LG, which I presume stands for 2.8 ltrs, Large Journal. Can anybody out there tell me if this block will accept the 3.1 crank that has the crank timing lobe on it? I have my block at the shop right now getting bored out and I need to order my kit. I want to go as big as I can but obviously don't want to waste my money. Thanks,||||reg||11
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||07-29-2000||08:15 PM||||Hey Brian, welcome to the forum!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I posted your email in another topic on the forum, you should get some replies pretty quickly, I know several people on here have done the 3.1 conversion before.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||07-29-2000||08:43 PM||||PDQ, basically, most 2.8 blocks produced from 1985 and newer will have the large journal main bearings. Since the block is in the shop, ask the machinist to mic (measure) the mains, if they are 67 mm, then you have the large journals, if they are 63 mm, then you have the small journals (which won't work, unless you have the 3.1 crank turned down). When you said, going as big as possible, I hope you don't mean boring it out to the max. I'd only go 0.030" or 0.040" overbore if possible. with the stroker crank, that puts displacement at about 3.2 liters.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pdqfiero||07-29-2000||09:57 PM||||Batboy, thanks for the responce but I think maybe you missed what I was trying to ask. I understand about the large journal/small journal thing. My question was with regard to the crank timing lobe that was added to the 3.1 crank that will interfere with some 2.8 large journal blocks. The article that I saw gave the specific block designators for the different year of Fiero that will work but mine was not listed. I was asking if anybody knew whether or not the list that I saw is all inclusive or if maybe the block that I have that is listed as 2.8 LG will still work. Thanks again for your help and I appreciate anybody elses comments. ||||reg||6
Z||000004||batboy||07-30-2000||12:11 AM||||Oh, never mind. Find a junk 3.1 crank in a salvage yard and trial fit it.||||reg||1
